This is a DIY house / shed notes repo, not a software app. Follow `.cursorrules` at the repo root as the project memory.

- Track progress in `TODO.md` checkboxes and dated `NOTES.md` bullets (newest first).
- Keep the layout at repo root: `README.md`, `TODO.md`, `NOTES.md`, `index.html` (progress site), `photos/`, `diagrams/`.
- **Always export a PNG when you create or edit an SVG** in `diagrams/` (1920px wide). Do not leave the PNG stale. Pair: `floor-plan.svg` → `floor-plan.png`, `sill-seal.svg` → `sill-seal.png`, `radiant-barrier.svg` → `radiant-barrier-diagram.png`.
- The progress site must keep reading `TODO.md` / `NOTES.md` live. Do not hardcode the checklist.
- Commit and push to `main`. Do not open a pull request unless the user asks.
- Do not reopen locked decisions in `.cursorrules` unless the user explicitly changes them.
- Nest under the gutters is gone (2026-09-21). Interior floor + walls in one corner cleaned 2026-09-25; mower still to walk out. Then probe the sill. Scrape nest remnants and reseat gutter guards when convenient.
- Cleanup before solar: battery lights/fan or a temporary outdoor GFCI cord — not AC or a swamp cooler.
- Interior photos (2026-09-03): sill plate is present; stud bottoms are moisture-stained — probe before sealing. Take lumber off the collar ties before the radiant barrier.
- Blue line on the roof OSB is the joint between wood roof parts and metal next to them. **Not a cable.** JPEG compression makes models invent staples and a jacket. Do not add a voltage-tester task.
- Back eave vents are in the flat soffit (confirmed 2026-09-25) and feed the back rafter bays to the ridge. Front gutter/eave has none. Don't block the back vents with foil or paint. They do not replace the room exhaust fan.
- Sill seal if salvageable: 1/4" hardware cloth in the wall-to-block gap + Z-flashing or PT/PVC skirt. Optional foam only behind the cloth. Point the downspout away from the corner. See diagrams/sill-seal.svg.
- Measured 2026-09-03/04: 16 ft eave × 12 ft gable, 87" top-of-wall to bottom-of-block, centered 48×75.5" double door with an 18×22" jalousie each side, 2×4×74" studs to the sheathing, 2×6 sill, double top plate, ~8.5" block. See diagrams/floor-plan.svg. Still need roof pitch and gap width.
